edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>African leaders herald $16B Dangote oil refinery in Kenya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bc21307b89a87d2cf296abed8e64d28691acb59b3fc941581828472c4b07edb</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:54:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/african-leaders-herald-16b-dangote-oil-refinery-in-kenya/a-79491068--44c455a72b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/african-leaders-herald-16b-dangote-oil-refinery-in-kenya/a-79491068?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An oil refinery on Kenya's coast is expected to be completed in 40 months, and will process an estimated 700,000 barrels of oil per day. Africa's richest man, Aliko Dangote, will lead the project.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>TV journalist is crowned king of Uganda's Tooro Kingdom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4ba0691bd509f11f1e2d61dc0e1f4717ceb062a517686c41361ce69ca0fa2e6</id><updated>2026-09-30T20:53:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tv-journalist-is-crowned-king-of-uganda-s-tooro-kingdom/a-79475911--6e0b4c2080aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tv-journalist-is-crowned-king-of-uganda-s-tooro-kingdom/a-79475911?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Edward Rukidi Kijanangoma has ascended to the throne after King Oyo died at the age of 34 due to a cancer battle. He previously worked for Ugandan broadcaster UBC as a TV anchor and editor.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
